KMSDRM: scaled fullscreen modes on the rotated DSI panel

Games that set their own video mode (dhewm3's r_mode, many ports) could
only get the panel's one mode. On top of the RGA rotation patch, offer
960x540, 854x480, 800x600, 640x480 and 640x360 as well: in exclusive
fullscreen the GBM surface gets that size, SDL reports it, and the RGA
pass that already rotates every frame scales it onto the panel, keeping
the aspect ratio (black bars for 4:3). The panel's mode does not change.
SDL_KMSDRM_SCALED_MODES=0 leaves the modes out.

